   "description": "The building then on the lot had been used as a fraternity house since the late 1920s, on a lot of about 6,600 square feet. It had 16 sleeping rooms, a large living room and a dining room, was for sale, and had been condemned by the Bureau of Building Inspection. The City Planning Commission disapproved, 6-1, converting the former fraternity house into a building of about twelve psychiatric offices.",
